[h1]D'thorga Vehicles[/h1]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.113.2
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published yet - draft held for the owner's review

[h2]Read this first (gotchas)[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Not yet tested in game[/b], except the survey truck and its boom, and the Busbar generator set's size and look.
[*][b]Needs Vehicle Framework and D'thorga Framework (0.169.0 or later)[/b], on [b]RimWorld 1.7 only[/b]. Load it after both; the mod asks for that order itself, so RimSort sorts it for you. Vanilla Expanded Framework is optional: it brings the garages.
[*][b]Safe to add to a running colony.[/b]
[*][b]Safe to remove only once none of its own vehicles is left.[/b] Scrap every tipper, tanker, drill rig, survey truck, generator set, seabed crawler, trailer and Osprey first, or they go with the mod. Pack up a set-up generator set, take every vehicle out of every garage, and empty and deconstruct every bulk bunker and loading chute. Other mods' vehicles go back to the general systems.
[*][b]Our vehicles are built from parts.[/b] Where RimThunder or Vanilla Vehicles Expanded is installed, a build asks for their parts; otherwise for ours, made at the vehicle parts bench. [b]Decide Parts for building in D'thorga Framework's settings before you start[/b]: it needs a restart.
[*][b]Each vehicle has its own research on the D'thorga tab[/b], after vehicle parts, and is built from the Architect's motor pool tab. Upgrades cost several hours' work and much steel and components, set by D'thorga Framework's Time to fit and tune and Materials to fit and tune.
[*][b]To set up a working vehicle, someone must be aboard and the engine running.[/b] A set-up vehicle cannot drive until you press Pack up. A trailer is set up and packed up by a colonist with construction work.
[*][b]Haulers fill a bulk bunker with chunks lying about the map[/b], as any stockpile that takes chunks: lower its priority or untick chunks to keep room for a truck. [b]A loading chute starts set to take nothing:[/b] tick what it should load.
[*][b]The five service trucks are armoured part by part[/b], as thin as a real civilian truck. Rifle fire hurts them more than before without Combat Extended. With Combat Extended each part is 2 mm of steel, and an armoured cab can take a spall liner. Armour kits come after truck armour research.
[*][b]Heavy trucks with air brakes must idle a few minutes[/b] after standing for hours before they will drive.
[*][b]A laden helicopter may refuse to lift off[/b] on a hot day or with an engine out; the launch button says why. A D'thorga Framework setting can allow it at a cost to the engine.
[*][b]The Lightning runs on chemfuel[/b] unless you turn on The Lightning runs on batteries in D'thorga Framework's settings (needs a restart).
[*][b]The water bowser exists only with Dubs Bad Hygiene[/b], and not in its lite mode.
[*][b]The Fathom seabed crawler is set aside for now:[/b] it is off the build menu. A boat already built keeps working.
[*][b]This mod has no settings of its own;[/b] it uses D'thorga Framework's vehicle settings.
[/list]

[h2]What it does[/h2]
Vehicles that keep running only while they are looked after. It adds working vehicles of its own, each with an upgrade tree, and gives the vehicles of other mods you already drive the systems that match what they really are.
[list]
[*][b]Datum survey truck:[/b] finds ore anywhere you can drive, ten times quicker than the game's scanner for a first find.
[*][b]Kelly drill rig:[/b] drills a found deposit at ten to thirty times a deep drill.
[*][b]Talus tipper truck:[/b] hauls 2,400 kg and tips it in one go. With its loading grab it gathers loose things you choose by itself, and delivers to storage you mark.
[*][b]Ullage bulk tanker:[/b] carries and pumps liquids and gases, and buys them in bulk at settlements.
[*][b]Busbar generator set:[/b] a 2,000 W power station you can drive away.
[*][b]Pintle trailers:[/b] a 5,000 kg flatbed, and water and fuel bowsers to leave at a camp.
[*][b]V-22 Osprey tiltrotor:[/b] two pilots, a crew chief and 24 seats, taking off straight up, with its own upgrades and guns.
[/list]

[b]Other mods' vehicles[/b] get their real counterparts' systems: air brakes on Vanilla Vehicles Expanded's Big Rig and RimThunder's HEMTT; gas turbines with their real lift limits on the Harrier, the A-10 and Su-25, the Hind, the Mongoose, the Cherokee, the Black Hawk and RimArrow's Ka-27PS and Mi-38; air-cooled turbines on the M1A2; steam locomotives (Trains of the Rim) that raise steam over hours and need water stops; real engines, weights and gearboxes on military vehicles; climate control on modern vehicles. Every other vehicle gets the general systems D'thorga Framework gives.

Every vehicle here has its own engine, door and work sounds. Its sounds and pictures were made with generative AI and picked by hand. How to play it is in the [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-rimworld/blob/main/docs/player-guide/working-vehicles.md]player guide's Working vehicles chapter[/url].

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*]RimWorld 1.7
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3014915404]Vehicle Framework[/url]
[*]D'thorga Framework, 0.169.0 or later
[/list]
Optional: Vanilla Expanded Framework (garages), Dubs Bad Hygiene (water bowser), Combat Extended.

